1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:17,930
X eight is the Nagel Point of triangle A B C: let N sub a, N sub b, and N sub c be the points where the three excircles touch sidelines B C, C A, and A B; the perimeter-bisecting cevians A N sub a, B N sub b, and C N sub c concur at X eight.

2
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:30,570
Its barycentric coordinates are directly proportional to the semiperimeter excesses, s minus a, to s minus b, to s minus c, and its trilinears are s minus a over a, to s minus b over b, to s minus c over c.

3
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:40,120
On the central lines layer, X eight anchors the Nagel line with X one, X two, and X ten, the Fuhrmann line with X four, and the Gergonne–Nagel line with X seven.

4
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:50,980
X eight is the isotomic conjugate of the Gergonne point X seven, the anticomplement of the Incenter X one, and the reflection of X one across the Spieker center X ten.
